        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 84-year-old male admitted on 26/05/2008 with acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and supportive intravenous fluids. Clinical response was satisfactory with improvement in oxygenation and symptom relief. He was discharged in stable condition with optimised inhaler therapy and a short course of oral steroids. Please arrange early follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Should you have any queries, please do not hesitate to contact me.</div>"
            },
